\section{On numerical stability}{

The binomial log-likelihood uses \code{logspace_add()} rather than
\code{log(1 + exp(eta))}. They are mathematically identical, but the naive form
overflows to infinity once \code{eta} exceeds about 709, which an optimiser can
easily reach while exploring. The stable form is exact throughout.
}

